# Every line here names something this repository can actually produce. A fence
# around a directory that does not exist reads as evidence the directory is
# expected, and the last set of those outlived the monorepo they were written
# for by several months.

# ── never track, anywhere ──
**/.credentials.json
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.token
.DS_Store

# ── written by running the tools in scripts/ ──
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
# scripts/build.py --out dist, and the same name in every plugin repository
dist/

# ── local to one machine, never to the repository ──
.claude/
.env
.env.*
*~
.*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── worktree machinery, managed by devtools:worktree ──
/.worktrees/

# ── agent-owned local context ──
/CLAUDE.local.md

# ── the plugin repositories somebody builds this against, and their baselines ──
# Foundry keeps no list of the plugins built with it, so the names of somebody's
# own repositories, and the file lists recorded from building them, stay on the
# machine that has them. .github/checks/repos.py explains the whole arrangement.
/.github/checks/repos.local
/.github/checks/baselines/local/
